# Timers are kept on the disk (/system/timers) and come back after a restart.
@disk
$ timer 1h bake bread
timer 1: 1h 00m (a window and a tune when it is up)
$ timer 2h
timer 2: 2h 00m (a window and a tune when it is up)
$ timer off 2
timer 2 cancelled
$ cat /system/timers
~ ^\d{10} bake bread$
@reboot
~ ^\[timer\] 1 timer\(s\) waiting, 0 missed while off
$ timers
~ ^  1 +(1h 00m|59m \d\ds) left  bake bread$
$ timer off 1
timer 1 cancelled
$ cat /system/timers
~ no such file
